 "_doc": "CHARACTER CUSTOMIZATION (per species). Sprites are recoloured at runtime (scripts/core/Look.gd), so every growth stage keeps the chosen look: SKIN picks the base colour (luminance of the original shading is kept, so the art still reads), PATTERN paints stripes/spots/mottling in PATTERN COLOUR on the skin pixels only, GENDER is cosmetic (crest tint) with no gameplay effect. 'sprites' lists every sprite that carries the look: skin_hue [lo,hi] (degrees) = which source hues count as skin; crest pixels are the red/orange hues; portrait=true sprites have a background that is flood-filled away from the borders and left untouched. A designer who paints real layered art can instead drop assets/sprites/<sprite>_skin.png / _pattern.png masks later: the options below keep their ids. Choice 'classic' + 'solid' + 'male' reproduces the original art exactly.",
